<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The two selection-menu items this library implements, as overridable and
  translatable Android resources.

  WHY THEY ARE RESOURCES AND NOT KOTLIN LITERALS. These strings are shown to
  the user, and until they lived here a French or Japanese app got "Copy
  Text" / "Copy Markdown" with no way to change them short of forking: the
  titles were `when`-branch literals with no Context in sight. As resources
  they get both Android override paths for free — a host app declares the
  same names in its own `res/values/strings.xml` (an app resource wins over a
  library's) to reword them, and adds `res/values-fr/strings.xml` to
  translate them.

  THE CROSS-PLATFORM PATH IS THE `title` FIELD, NOT THIS FILE. These are the
  FALLBACK, used for a `selectionActions` entry that is a bare identifier.
  An entry written as `{ id, title }` in JS carries its own label, which
  reaches Android and iOS alike from whatever i18n the app already uses; see
  src/view/selectionActions.ts. This file is what makes the Android half
  overridable for an app that would rather stay in Android resources — the
  counterpart of the iOS host's NSLocalizedString lookup against Bundle.main.

  The names are prefixed because a library's resources merge into the
  application's single namespace, where a plain `copy_text` would be a
  collision waiting to happen — and, since an app resource silently wins, a
  collision that renames this menu rather than failing the build.
-->
<resources>
    <string name="selectable_markdown_copy_text">Copy Text</string>
    <string name="selectable_markdown_copy_markdown">Copy Markdown</string>
</resources>
